# Optional programs and safety limits

Add an external program through `runCommand`. Do not build a shell string. Do not execute Nmap or read Nmap data files (`docs/adr/006-native-service-inspection.md` supersedes ADR 003).

1. Add the smallest method on the consumer port (`app.ToolRunner` in `internal/app/ports.go`).
2. Implement it in `internal/adapter/tools` with `runCommand`: fixed argv, a context deadline, stdout and stderr caps, and process-group or Windows Job Object cancellation (`prepareCommand`).
3. Discover the binary with `exec.LookPath`. Missing is `dependency_missing`. An out-of-range version is `unsupported`. Do not vendor the executable.
4. Reject oversized or out-of-scope parser output. History stores provider version and counts, not targets, probe text, packet payloads, or Wi-Fi keys.
5. Call it from `app.Application`, then from Wails, HTTP, and the CLI through `internal/adapter/contract`. Add `en` and `pt` strings.
6. Extend `internal/porttest` and `internal/porttest/fake`.

Service inspection is native TCP, banner, TLS and one HTTP request: an explicit IPv4 /24 or narrower, at most 32 ports, and a two-minute deadline. TShark 4.2+ within major 4 is inventory-only.

Wi-Fi reveal is explicit (`wifi reveal --confirm` or the desktop action) and the displayed secret is cleared. Capture starts only on request, never at launch. `serve` binds loopback unless `--allow-remote` is set together with TLS. Do not log launch tokens or session cookies.
